*(Teacher: Can it not be done via inference? But perceptions... it is not perception. Is it not perception? Just like we get "The mountain possesses fire" [even when fire isn't directly seen]. But here, isn't silver seen by the eye? Therefore, silver is an object of direct perception... Hence, it cannot be established through inference.)*



